    "intro_html":  "Pollo saltado is what happened when Chinese immigrants brought wok cooking to Peru in the 1800s, and Peruvians call the whole cuisine chifa. It is a soy and vinegar stir fry with onions, tomatoes and aji amarillo, and then, because this is Peru, it gets served over rice with french fries thrown right in the pan. Yes, both starches. It sounds like a dare and it works. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
